About this step: you're fitting. Each spectrum Part 2 handed you is full of mode
peaks, and hidden in each peak are the three numbers we're after: the frequency,
the linewidth, and the amplitude. A peak is never alone though, it sits in a
thicket of leaks from neighboring modes, so the fitter models the whole crowd at
once and reads the target cleanly. That's what keeps the numbers honest. Of the
three, the linewidth is the one that's barely been used, and it's the one this
group is going after.
